  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-127239",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Our second-degree Taylor polynomial is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{2}(x) & =6-5(x-3)-3(x-3)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can approximate $f(3.2)$ by evaluating the second-degree Taylor polynomial approximation at $x=3.2.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3.2) & ≈{P}_{2}(3.2) \\\\  & =6-5(3.2-3)-3(3.2-3)^{2} \\\\  & =6-5(0.2)-3(0.2)^{2} \\\\  & =4.88.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
